# NewsLens environment — copy to `.env` (cp .env.example .env) and fill it in
# YOURSELF. Names + descriptions only live in this file; real values only ever
# live in .env, which is gitignored. Never paste a key into chat or a commit —
# if one leaks, rotate it at the provider immediately.
#
# After filling anything in, run `scripts/doctor` — it validates every value
# with harmless read-only calls and tells you exactly what's still missing.

# --- LLM generation (required) -----------------------------------------------
# Text generation (GPT-4o-mini) for the ranking / narrative / script steps.
# Get one at platform.openai.com/api-keys. Scope: standard API key, no special
# permissions beyond default usage — and set a hard monthly spend cap in the
# OpenAI dashboard (Settings -> Limits), not just in-app.
# NOTE on audio: the default TTS is gpt-4o-mini-tts on THIS key (~$0.015/min,
# ~+$0.07/run — your ear-test pick, 2026-07-06). Kokoro-82M local stays fully
# built as the $0 fallback: pin `settings.tts_engine: kokoro` in sources.yaml
# to use it. This key is needed for text generation regardless of the voice.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# --- Claude provider seam (B3: rank/editor/script DEFAULT to the subscription
#     lane; ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is now the API FALL-OVER credential) -------------
# B3 flipped rank/editor/script to the `claude -p` subscription lane by default
# (subscription is ALWAYS the priority; the API lane is their registered
# fall-over). Those seats now need the CLI installed + logged in, NOT the key —
# see SETUP.md "Install the Claude CLI" and NEWSLENS_CLAUDE_BIN below.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is required only when a seat runs the API lane: you pin one
# with NEWSLENS_LANE_<SEAT>=api, or you arm NEWSLENS_LANE_FALLBACK=api. Get one
# at console.anthropic.com/settings/keys; set a hard monthly cap. Never logged.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# NEWSLENS_CLAUDE_BIN overrides where the subscription lane finds the `claude`
# CLI. Resolution order: NEWSLENS_CLAUDE_BIN -> PATH -> ~/.local/bin/claude. The
# doctor reports which resolved; a missing binary FAILs the run naming the fix.
# Set this only if the CLI isn't on PATH and isn't at the default location.
NEWSLENS_CLAUDE_BIN=
# Lane selection for the provider seam (all optional; unset = the default seat
# map in llm.SEATS — EVERY anthropic seat on the SUBSCRIPTION lane: writer,
# analyst, editor, script and state on Claude Opus 4.8; rank and the
# follow-altitude resolver on Claude Sonnet 5. `synthesis` (GPT-4o, api) is the
# only openai seat left and it has no live call site).
# NEWSLENS_LANE = api | subscription (global); NEWSLENS_LANE_<SEAT> (e.g.
# NEWSLENS_LANE_RANK) overrides one seat. Selecting a lane with no registered
# provider — or a subscription seat with no resolvable CLI — FAILS LOUD naming
# the fix (never a silent wrong-lane call). NEWSLENS_LANE_FALLBACK=api is the
# principal-armed opt-in that lets an unavailable subscription seat fall ONCE to
# the api lane (spends real API money the subscription lane would not — the ship
# checkpoint asks whether to arm it). Leave all unset in normal operation.
NEWSLENS_LANE=
NEWSLENS_LANE_FALLBACK=
# NEWSLENS_MODEL_<SEAT> — the ~07-24 BATTERY HARNESS surface ONLY (scripts/battery
# sets it per arm): swaps just the model string for one seat (e.g.
# NEWSLENS_MODEL_WRITER=claude-fable-5 to run the Fable arm of the blind writer
# A/B) while provider/lane/thinking/effort/prices stay the seat's. UNSET in
# normal operation — a stray value silently reprices/re-models an edition.
NEWSLENS_MODEL_WRITER=

# --- Discovery beyond named sources (required for Tier 2 sourcing) ------------
# Perplexity Sonar API for the one capped discovery query per run ("what's
# happening today that isn't in my named sources"). Get one at
# perplexity.ai/settings/api. Pay-as-you-go — set a prepaid credit cap in the
# Perplexity dashboard as the real spend limit; BUDGET_CAP_USD_PER_RUN below
# is a secondary guard, not the primary one.
# Until this key exists, ingest runs RSS-only and says so — and the moment it
# lands, run `scripts/sonar_spike` (the pending reliability gate).
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=

# --- Cost guardrails (required, no external account needed) -------------------
# Aborts any LLM-spending run (rank today; generate at M5) whose estimated
# cost exceeds this (USD).
# ENGINEERING.md-mandated guardrail against runaway/retry-loop costs.
# Unset = default 1.50 (B4 2026-07-16: raised from 0.25 because the writer flipped
# to Opus 4.8 and the analyst to Sonnet 5 — the GPT-4o-era 0.25 aborted every
# edition at the narrative pre-check. Approved shadow envelope ~$0.90-1.30/edition;
# the shadow is undiscounted, so the cap over-counts — the safe direction. See
# config.py; TUNE DOWN once measured spend lands).
BUDGET_CAP_USD_PER_RUN=1.50

# --- Scheduling (LIVE since NL-146; dormant 2026-07-03 -> 2026-08-13) ---------
# The local hour (0-23) a SCHEDULED run fires at. Unset = 6 (06:00 local).
# `newslens schedule plist` bakes this hour into the launchd agent, so changing
# it means re-rendering and re-bootstrapping (SETUP.md section 5). On-demand
# `newslens generate` ignores this entirely. NOT a new variable — this one has
# been here, and unread, since 2026-07-03.
GENERATE_HOUR_LOCAL=6

# --- The phone (NL-163 Stage A) — optional, both or neither -------------------
# Where this machine DELIVERS the frozen edition it mints at every publish, and
# the token that authorises the delivery. Leave both blank and nothing changes:
# editions are still frozen to data/briefings/<date>.phone.json and readable
# with `newslens bundle --open` — they are simply delivered nowhere.
#
# The URL names the STREAM (one paper per token):
#   NEWSLENS_PUSH_URL=https://<your host>/api/streams/main
# The host stores only sha256(token), so the value below is the only copy of
# the token that exists. Mint one, and its digest, with the two commands in
# hosted/DEPLOY.md. A failed push NEVER costs an edition: the artifact stays on
# disk and `newslens push --date <d>` re-sends it. `newslens doctor` reports
# the delivery state of every frozen edition.
NEWSLENS_PUSH_URL=
NEWSLENS_PUSH_TOKEN=

# --- The phone door (NL-163 Stage A M3) — THE OPERATOR'S HALF, this machine ---
# These two create readers' accounts and nothing else. They are the only vendor
# credentials that exist anywhere in this product, and they live HERE, on the
# machine that makes the paper — never on the host that serves it.
#
#   STYTCH_PROJECT_ID  the project those accounts belong to. Starts with
#                      `project-test-` or `project-live-`; that prefix is what
#                      tells `newslens phone-account` which environment to call,
#                      so it is never guessed. Dashboard -> API Keys.
#   STYTCH_SECRET      the project secret. Used by ONE command
#                      (`newslens phone-account`), sent in one Authorization
#                      header, never printed, never logged, never written to
#                      disk, never given to the host. If it ever appears in a
#                      chat or a screenshot, rotate it in the dashboard.
#
# Leave both blank and nothing breaks: the paper still generates, freezes and
# delivers. What you cannot do without them is create a reader.
#   newslens phone-account create <email> --stream main            (dry run)
#   newslens phone-account create <email> --stream main --commit   (for real)
# `newslens doctor` reports which half is configured, by NAME only.
STYTCH_PROJECT_ID=
STYTCH_SECRET=

# --- The phone door — THE HOST'S HALF (these go on the SERVER, not here) ------
# Listed in this file so the deploy runbook is not a guess; they belong in
# `fly secrets set` / the host's environment, and setting them here does
# nothing at all. THE HOST HOLDS NO VENDOR SECRET — every name below is public.
#
#   NEWSLENS_STYTCH_PROJECT_ID    the same project id as above (public)
#   NEWSLENS_STYTCH_PUBLIC_TOKEN  the PUBLISHABLE token the sign-in page uses
#   NEWSLENS_STYTCH_JWKS_URL      where the host reads the vendor's public keys
#                                 (defaults to the documented URL for this
#                                 project; override only to pin a mirror)
#   NEWSLENS_STYTCH_JWKS          OPTIONAL — the key set pasted verbatim
#                                 (`newslens phone-account jwks` prints it).
#                                 Set it and the reading path opens no socket to
#                                 anyone; costs a re-paste at each ~6-month key
#                                 rotation.
#   NEWSLENS_STYTCH_SDK_URL       the sign-in SDK the login page loads. SET IT
#                                 — do not take the default. M4 fetched the
#                                 default artifact and found it MISSING two of
#                                 the methods the page calls (the password arm
#                                 throws; the silent session refresh never
#                                 fires). Use the URL your project's dashboard
#                                 names. hosted/DEPLOY.md, 'THE SDK ARTIFACT
#                                 DOES NOT MATCH THE ADAPTER'.
#   NEWSLENS_STYTCH_ISSUER        OPTIONAL — the expected `iss` claim. Defaults
#                                 to `stytch.com/<project id>`
#   NEWSLENS_STYTCH_AUDIENCE      OPTIONAL — the expected `aud` claim. Defaults
#                                 to the project id
#   NEWSLENS_USER_STREAMS         {"<user id>": "<stream>"} — one account reads
#                                 one paper. `newslens phone-account create`
#                                 prints the exact row to add.
# Full runbook: SETUP.md, 'The phone door', and hosted/DEPLOY.md.

# --- Optional fallback (not required for the v1 default path) -----------------
# Fallback discovery source ONLY if the Sonar reliability spike fails (that
# spike is still pending). Leave blank until then — narrowest-scope rule:
# don't grant a second paid API key while the primary is unproven-insufficient.
GNEWS_API_KEY=
